# ===========================================================================
# ABNY / «ابني» — CHILD APP RELEASE SIGNING TEMPLATE
#
# Copy this file to `signing.properties` IN THIS DIRECTORY and fill in the four
# values. `signing.properties` is gitignored (see android/.gitignore); this
# template is committed. NEVER put real passwords in this file.
#
#     cp signing.properties.example signing.properties
#
# app/build.gradle reads it. If it is absent and a release task is scheduled,
# the build FAILS with an actionable message — it does NOT fall back to the
# debug keystore. That fallback is what made every previous "release" artifact
# unuploadable (docs/release/STORE_READINESS.md row 5).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. GENERATE THE UPLOAD KEYSTORE (once, on a machine you control)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Requires the JDK's `keytool` (JDK 17 — the version this project pins).
# Run it from THIS directory (apps/child-app/android/):
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v \
#     -keystore abny-child-upload.jks \
#     -alias abny-child-upload \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000 \
#     -storetype PKCS12
#
# Notes on every flag, because each one is a decision:
#   -keystore   the file this properties file's `storeFile` must name. Keep it
#               OUT of the repository if you can; `*.jks` here is gitignored,
#               but a backup you control is the only copy that matters.
#   -alias      referenced by `keyAlias` below. Write it down: an alias you
#               cannot remember is a lost key.
#   -keysize    4096. Play accepts 2048; 4096 costs nothing at signing time.
#   -validity   10000 days (~27 years). Play REQUIRES an upload key valid past
#               22 October 2033. A shorter validity is accepted at upload and
#               then blocks you later.
#   -storetype  PKCS12. The old JKS format still works but keytool warns on
#               every use and it is being phased out.
#
# keytool will prompt for a store password, a key password and a distinguished
# name. Use DIFFERENT store and key passwords. Store all three in your password
# manager — see the LOSS section at the bottom.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. THE FOUR VALUES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `storeFile` is resolved RELATIVE TO apps/child-app/android/ (this
# directory), so the plain filename below works. An absolute path also works
# and is the better choice if you keep the keystore outside the working tree.
storeFile=abny-child-upload.jks

# The -storepass you gave keytool.
storePassword=CHANGE_ME_store_password

# The -alias you gave keytool.
keyAlias=abny-child-upload

# The -keypass you gave keytool (different from storePassword).
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME_key_password

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. BUILDING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   flutter build appbundle --release \
#     --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api/v1
#
# The AAB lands at build/app/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab — that is
# the file Play accepts. `flutter build apk --release` still works and produces
# a sideloadable APK for QA, but Play has not accepted APKs for new apps since
# August 2021.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. CI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .github/workflows/build-apk.yml writes this exact file from repository
# secrets and then deletes the keystore in a post step. The secrets are
# per-app, because the two apps are two Play listings:
#
#   ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64_CHILD   base64 of the .jks
#                                    (`base64 -w0 abny-child-upload.jks`)
#   ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD_CHILD
#   ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS_CHILD
#   ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD_CHILD
#
# Every one of them is required for a release run; a missing secret turns the
# job RED. It never degrades to a debug-signed artifact.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. WHAT LOSING THIS KEY COSTS — READ BEFORE YOU FIRST UPLOAD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENROL IN PLAY APP SIGNING (the default for new apps). Google then holds the
# APP signing key and this keystore is only the UPLOAD key, which Google can
# reset for you if you lose it. That single choice converts "the app is dead
# and must be republished under a new package name, losing every install,
# review and rating" into a support ticket.
#
# If you opt OUT of Play App Signing, losing this file is terminal: no future
# update to com.aifamilycoach.child_app can ever be published.
#
# The applicationId this key will be bound to at first upload is
# `com.aifamilycoach.child_app` — and that name is still an OPEN HUMAN
# DECISION (PROJECT_STATUS.md §0's EBNEY/ABNY question, and
# docs/release/IOS_READINESS.md). Settle it BEFORE the first upload: the
# package name is immutable afterwards.
